00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:27,360
虽说翻车的概率本来就更高。
Which is more likely to happen.

301
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,440
但事实摆在眼前，
But the fact of the matter is,

302
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,720
就像我们刚才看到的，
as we saw earlier,

303
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:31,440
大块头的高车在撞车时就是占优势。
big tall cars are better in crashes.

304
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:33,400
正面撞、追尾撞、侧面撞，
Frontal impact, rear impact, side impact.

305
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,840
坐这种车里准没错。
You're better off with one of these.

306
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:36,080
绝佳的被动安全。
Good passive safety.

307
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:37,640
最现实的道理就是，
The simple fact of the matter is,

308
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:40,120
要是让我挑个地方塞我自己的孩子，
if I wanted to put my children anywhere,

309
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:41,720
我肯定把他们塞进这辆车里。
I'd put them in one of these.

310
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,200
因为说到底，保命赢面更大。
- 没错。
'Cause basically, the odds are better.
- Yeah.

311
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,760
好了，说车重。我们《Top Gear》
对车重向来有种执念。
Right, weight. We've got a thing
about weight on  Top Gear.

312
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:47,640
前几天晚上我们在小酒馆里还聊起这事。
We were talking about
this the other night in the pub.

313
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:50,080
我们发现现在的车是越造越沉，
We noticed that cars are getting heavier

314
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:53,360
但在我们赛道上刷出最快圈速的，
全都是轻量化快车。
and yet the fastest cars
around our track were light.

315
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,720
显而易见，车子越重，跑得就越慢。
Clearly, the heavier they are,
the slower they're going to be.

316
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:58,200
而且油耗越高，用车成本就越贵。
And the more fuel they're going to use,
the more they'll cost to run.

317
00:14:58,240 --> 00:15:01,440
所以我们就琢磨：要是找来
一台普普通通的笨重家用车，
So we thought, what if you took
a normal heavy car

318
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,560
然后把所有多余没用的零碎全拆下来，
and then took out of it all the spare stuff

319
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:05,280
彻底给它偷轻减重，
that you don't need to make it lighter.

320
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:07,240
它到底能快上多少？
How much faster could you make it go?

321
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:08,960
行吧，我们总得弄个明白。
Well, we had to find out.

322
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,360
鉴于BBC独特的经费运作方式，
Because of the unique way the BBC's funded,

323
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:14,480
我们只有500镑预算，
于是就搞来了这台货。
we had a budget of 500 quid
and got us this.

324
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:17,960
没错，一台1985年的捷豹XJS V12。
Yep, it's a 1985 Jaguar XJS V12.

325
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:21,360
5.3升发动机，300匹制动马力。
5.3-litre engine, 300 brake horsepower.

326
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,400
刚才，我们让斯提格
开着它出去跑了一圈，
Now, earlier on, we sent
The Stig out in this,

327
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:27,600
他跑出了惊人的0到60英里加速：
8.6秒。
and he clocked up a remarkable 0-60 time
of 8.6 seconds.

328
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:45,200
这车在当年可不算慢，
This car wasn't slow in its day,

329
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:47,080
放到现在也依然挺快的。
and it's still pretty quick.

330
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:48,160
好吧，但如果……
Okay, but what would happen

331
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,560
我们给它减个肥会怎样？
if we put it on a diet.

332
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,560
尽可能把能拆的重量全扒光。
If we strip out as much weight as we can.

333
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:54,400
它会跑得更快吗？得，这帮人
就是来干这个的。
Will it go any faster? Well, that's what
this lot are here for.

334
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:55,960
伙计们，他们可是打康沃尔来的。
Guys, they've come from Cornwall.

335
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,720
那是你的老地盘，
所以你大概……
That's your stamping ground,
so you'll probably

336
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:59,320
……能听得懂
他们在叨叨些什么。
kind of understand
what they're talking about.

337
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:01,200
没错，要是聊崩了我也能翻译。
Yes I can translate if it gets messy.

338
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,520
那敢情好。那先开始吧，
That's useful. Well, to start,

339
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:03,960
你能不能叫他们赶紧开工？
can you just tell 'em to crack on?

340
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,560
行。麻利干起来！
Okay. Crack on!

341
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:12,440
好嘞。这事进展如何，
待会儿节目里见分晓，
Right. We'll see how that gets
on later on in the show,

342
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:14,480
但眼下，我们碰上个大麻烦。
but for now, we've got a problem.

343
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:16,120
说来听听。
- 斯提格说
Go on.
- The Stig is saying

344
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:19,120
他不想再开车兜圈子了，
因为他想打广告宣传……
he doesn't want to drive around
because he wants to promote...

345
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:20,840
他自己录了张CD，懂了吧？
He's done this CD, okay?

346
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,800
算是一张他的轻音乐
“圣诞金曲合辑”。
A sort of "Christmas Hits"
of his easy listening.

347
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,320
他想宣传这玩意儿，但我们说了：
And he wants to promote it, and we've said,

348
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,240
“这里可是BBC，你休想打广告。”
"It's the BBC, you can't promote it."

349
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:29,280
哈蒙德：对头。
- 所以他现在耍小脾气了。
HAMMOND: Yep.
- So he's having a strop.

350
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,800
呃，一个发飙的斯提格。
克拉克森：没错。
Uh, a cross Stig.
CLARKSON: Yes.

351
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:32,080
道威：绝不妥协。
哈蒙德：合情合理。
DAWE: Don't give in.
HAMMOND: Fair enough.

352
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:33,800
不管怎样，先来看《新闻栏目》吧，
Anyway, let's do The News,

353
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,400
让制片人们去头疼那事吧。
and let the producers worry about that one.

354
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:39,520
呃，赶上圣诞节，
这周其实没啥新车上市。
Um, and no new product, really,
this week, it being Christmas.

355
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:41,400
嗯，不过可聊的猛料多得是。
Um, but there's plenty to talk about.

356
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:42,960
当然，最重磅的一条就是：
Most important of all, of course,

357
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,280
雅克·库斯托在英吉利海峡
Jacques Cousteau opened a dealership

358
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:47,820
开了家汽车经销商。[笑声]
（三色号货轮相撞沉没 - 2002年12月14日）
in the English Channel. [LAUGHTER]
(MV Tricolor collision - 14/12/2002)

359
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:48,960
没错，这是……
Yeah, this is...

360
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,240
[观众鼓掌]
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDING]

361
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,920
这就是沉了的那艘货轮。
This is the boat that's gone down.

362
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:56,880
上面装了多少，三千辆车左右？
What, is it 3,000 cars,
something like that?

363
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:58,080
整整三千辆！
3,000 cars!

364
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,720
有意思的是，绝大部分是宝马，
Interestingly, mostly BMW,

365
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:03,480
你一听就知道它绝对是艘“宝马船”，
and you just knew it had to be a BMW boat,

366
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:06,040
因为一开到海峡它就直接猛拐变道，连左右看都不看一眼。
'cause it got to the channel and just
pulled out, didn't look left or right.

367
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:07,880
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

368
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,560
然后，轰的一声巨响。
And, big impact.

369
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,200
两艘大船撞在一块儿，看着都肉疼。
Two ships collide. That's got to hurt.

370
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,440
接着就往海底沉。
“咣当”一声砸在海底。
Then it sinks to the bottom.
Clunk hits the bottom.

371
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:14,960
又是剧烈一撞。
Another big impact.

372
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,400
整整三千辆车啊。
3,000 cars.

373
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,960
为什么那些安全气囊没全弹开呢？
Why didn't all the airbags go off?

374
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,080
因为要是全弹开了，
整艘船不就“嗖”的一下……
Because if they had,
it would have just, whoop...

375
00:17:20,120 --> 00:17:21,840
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

376
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,600
浮上来了，问题解决。
Problem solved.

377
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:25,360
当然现在的实际情况是，
它正老老实实躺在海底呢，
Of course the thing is,
it's now lying on the bottom,

378
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:27,840
而你们也了解那些西班牙渔民。
and you know all the Spanish fishermen.

379
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,040
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

380
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:30,640
你们猜到接下来会怎样了吧？
You know what's coming now, don't you?

381
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:32,760
既然自家海岸线全被原油给糟蹋了，
'Cause their coastline
has been wrecked by all the oil,

382
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:34,280
他们肯定一路直奔英吉利海峡，
they'll be straight up the English Channel,

383
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:37,000
一网捞起两辆宝马318来。
hooking themselves a couple of 318s up.

384
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:39,560
“哟，瞧瞧捞着了什么！”
- 也不全是宝马吧，
不还有萨博吗？
"Ooh, look at that!"
- They're not all BMWs,
are they? Saabs as well.

385
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,720
所以他们就会说：
“哎，把那个扔回去。”
- “扔回海里。”
So they'll be like,
"Oh, chuck that back."
- Throw it back.

386
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:44,920
[西班牙口音]“一辆萨博9-3？我才不要，
补贴给得不够多！”
[SPANISH ACCENT] "A 9-3? I don't want it.
Not subsidised enough."

387
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:46,440
真正惨绝人寰的是那台沃尔沃，
The true disaster is that Volvo,

388
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:48,800
就是我们刚才聊的那款XC90，是吧？
the XC90, which we've just looked at, yeah?

389
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,360
那可是台好车。
Great car.

390
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:51,720
他们一年满打满算也就造五万辆，
They're only making 50,000 of 'em
a year anyway,

391
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:53,480
本来就严重供不应求。
- 嗯哼。
which is not enough.
- Mmm-hmm.

392
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:55,280
结果有三百五十辆都在那艘船上！
Three hundred and fifty of them
were on the boat!

393
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:56,240
克拉克森：不会吧！
- 是的。
CLARKSON: No!
- Yeah.

394
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:58,280
全沉了！
- 三百五十辆？！
They've sunk!
- 350?

395
00:17:58,320 --> 00:17:59,760
这下提车更遥遥无期了。
It's gonna make it worse.

396
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,040
哈蒙德：想象一下那通电话：“喂，我的车呢？”
HAMMOND: Imagine that phone call,
"Where's my car?"

397
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,000
“呃，这个嘛……”
[笑声]
Well, um...
[LAUGHTER]

398
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,080
“我潜下海底找雅克问问看。”
"I'll pop down and see Jacques."

399
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:05,920
所以你要是真想要一辆XC90，
if you want an XC90,

400
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:08,200
直接去一趟西班牙北部海域吧，好吗？
pop over to Northern Spain, okay?

401
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:09,480
虽然泡了点水受损，
Slightly water-damaged,

402
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:10,240
但它们早晚都得落得这下场。
but that's where they'll all end up.

403
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,600
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

404
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:12,720
绝无悬念。
Almost certainly.

405
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:14,560
呃，摩根汽车，
Um, Morgan,

406
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:16,440
他们又要重返赛场了，
这是个好消息，替他们高兴。
they're going racing again,
which is good news. Good for them.

407
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:17,800
但显然赛车这行当烧钱得很，
But it's an expensive business, obviously,

408
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:19,400
眼下经济又在衰退。
recession on the way.

409
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,480
画面上是他们在勒芒的赛车，
这游戏可真烧钱。
There's their car at Le Mans,
it's a very expensive game.

410
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:23,880
而且现在赞助根本拉不到，
经济衰退又步步逼近，
And sponsorship is hard to come by,
recession on the way,

411
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:25,200
所以他们想出了个好点子，
so they've come up with a good idea

412
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:26,920
来筹几个小钱凑够跑比赛的开销。
to raise a few quid to do this.

413
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:29,640
这么解释最贴切，
你们还记得《比诺》（Beano）俱乐部吗？
Best way to explain it.
Do you remember the Beano Club?

414
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:31,040
你们入过会吗？当年入会要花……
Did you join that? It cost...

415
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:32,880
还是说只有我……就我一个人入过，是吧？
Or was it just... it's just me, isn't it?

416
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,120
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

417
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:35,600
反正我还记得，
Well, I remember it,

418
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:37,400
大概花你5便士，把申请寄过去，
and it cost you about 5p, and you sent off,

419
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,640
然后你就会收到一张小会员卡，
and you got a little membership card,

420
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:41,040
还有一个带凸眼球的小徽章。
and a badge with little googly eyes on it.

421
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:43,560
于是呢，摩根也推出了
So, Morgan have launched

422
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:45,200
“摩根俱乐部”，你也能加入。
the Morgan Club, and you can join this.

423
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:46,920
虽然比5便士稍微贵了那么一点点，
It is a bit more expensive than 5p,

424
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:47,880
要1000英镑。
it's £1,000.

425
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,360
嚯！
Ooh.

426
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:51,840
是的，但这笔钱能换来，呃……
Yes, but for that, you do get, uh...

427
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,160
这能帮到……这基本上就是拿来代替赞助商的？
And this helps... that's basically instead
of sponsorship?

428
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:55,240
他们就是拉大家……
They just get people...

429
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,800
所有人都来入会，一人一千镑。
All these people join, £1,000.

430
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:58,040
钱全凑进公账，
他们就能去跑比赛了。
That goes in the kitty,
so they can go racing.

431
00:18:58,080 --> 00:18:59,800
行，明白了。
- 掏了这一千镑，
Right, okay.
- And for your £1,000,

432
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,320
你得自己开车去赛道，
you drive yourself over to the circuit,

433
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:02,520
显而易见，去现场看比赛。
obviously, to go and watch the racing.

434
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,120
但等你到了那儿，要是你还记得这茬，
But when you get there, if you remember,

435
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:07,000
你就能进赛道，
并且在大看台上占个座。
you get entrance to the circuit
and a seat in the grandstand.

436
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:08,200
座位？
哈蒙德：对。
Seat?
HAMMOND: Yeah.

437
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,440
什么样式的座？
What sort of seat?

438
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,080
大概就是个红色塑料板凳。
It'll be like a red plastic thing.

439
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:12,720
所以不是王座喽？
- 不是。
Not a throne, then?
- No.

440
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:14,080
花一千镑我可得要个王座才行，
Which is what I'd want for £1,000,

441
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,960
铺着虎皮。
with tiger skin.

442
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,520
哈蒙德：头顶还得拉个遮阳棚，
旁边有人给你扇扇子。
HAMMOND: Sun screen over the top
with somebody fanning you.

443
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,760
还得有几个半裸的斐济姑娘伺候我纳凉。
Some half-naked Fijian girls chilling me.

444
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,440
不，上面可一个字都没提这些，杰里米。
No, it doesn't say anything
about any of that, Jeremy.

445
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:23,880
没有吗？好吧。
- 但你的名字可以写在
No? Okay.
- But you do get to put your name

446
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:26,640
一份名单上，跟其他同样
给摩根送了一千英镑的冤大头列在一起。
on a list of other people
who've given Morgan £1,000.

447
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:29,000
你还能获得近距离接触车队的特权，
You get private access to the team, which,

