00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:33,200
超低重心彻底消除了普通越野车那种晃晃悠悠的开船感。
That low centre of gravity helps cut out
the usual off-roader wobbliness.

595
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:37,600
开着足够文明体面，下地越野也毫不露怯。
It's civilised, but without losing
the ability to cut it off-road.

596
00:26:39,360 --> 00:26:41,280
至于缺点嘛，这玩意儿是个油老虎，
On the downside, it is thirsty,

597
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:43,400
而且这内饰嘛，呃……
and the interior is, uh...

598
00:26:43,440 --> 00:26:45,880
在装潢审美上真谈不上有半点灵感。
Well, not exactly inspired
in terms of decor.

599
00:26:45,920 --> 00:26:50,760
不过上一代森林人的车厢简直灾难，而这一代至少不辣眼睛。
But then the previous Forester
was truly awful inside, and this one isn't.

600
00:26:50,800 --> 00:26:52,240
所以，倒也算件好事。
So that's good.

601
00:26:52,280 --> 00:26:54,920
这收音机很明显就是
冲着翼豹买家设计的。
The radio is clearly aimed
at buyers of the Impreza.

602
00:26:54,960 --> 00:26:57,360
上面有一大堆密密麻麻的小按键，
It's got loads of tiny little buttons

603
00:26:57,400 --> 00:26:59,360
一到晚上亮起来跟个海上钻井平台似的。
and it lights up like an old rig at night.

604
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:01,240
但声音贼大，所以这点也挺不错。
But it is dead loud, so that's good, too.

605
00:27:01,260 --> 00:27:04,260
♪ Dirty Vegas - I Should Know ♪
♪ Dirty Vegas - I Should Know ♪

606
00:27:04,600 --> 00:27:09,040
所以他们把涡轮增压翼豹的基因
塞进了一辆家用车里，
So they put the DNA of an Impreza turbo
into a family car,

607
00:27:09,080 --> 00:27:11,080
而且还真神了！
and it works!

608
00:27:11,120 --> 00:27:14,000
森林人可不是那种
张扬跋扈的硬派越野车，
It's not an in-your-face
off-roader, the Forester.

609
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:16,240
比起 CR-V、神行者、
compared to CR-Vs, Freelanders,

610
00:27:16,280 --> 00:27:17,680
RAV4 之类的车，
Rav4s and the like.

611
00:27:17,720 --> 00:27:20,080
它看着，呃，可能略显低调了点。
It looks, well, perhaps a little bit quiet.

612
00:27:20,120 --> 00:27:21,640
但相信我，
But believe me,

613
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:24,160
它绝对是这群车里最棒的。
it really is the best of the bunch.

614
00:27:26,640 --> 00:27:28,200
你知道森林人还有哪点好吗？
You know the other thing
about the Forester?

615
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:30,000
斯巴鲁总能、永远能
Subaru always, always win

616
00:27:30,040 --> 00:27:32,080
在那些可靠性调查里拿第一。
- 没错，绝对是这样。
those reliability surveys.
- That's true, absolutely.

617
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:34,040
所以这也算它的一大加分项，
So you got that in its favour,

618
00:27:34,080 --> 00:27:35,120
更别说家用方面它啥都能搞定。
and the fact that it'll do
everything you want for the family.

619
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:36,760
它跑得飞快，
It is very quick,

620
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:39,040
又不会像那种高头大马的四驱SUV一样容易翻车。
and it won't fall over like a tall 4x4.

621
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:43,080
一点没错。而且最爽的是，照片来了。
Exactly. And, best thing of all,
here's a photograph.

622
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:46,800
它得上咱们板子上的“酷”区！
- 噢，没错，必须贴那儿。
It goes in the Cool section of our board!
- Oh, yes, it does.

623
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:49,480
对，很酷的车。
克拉克森：说不酷是什么意思？
Yeah, cool car.
CLARKSON: What do you mean, no?

624
00:27:49,520 --> 00:27:51,320
胡说！
克拉克森：等等。
Wrong!
CLARKSON: Hold on.

625
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:53,200
你瞧过那内饰吗？
- 瞧过啊。
Have you seen the interior?
- Yes.

626
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:55,840
拜托，又平庸又无聊又寡淡。
Well, it's bland and boring and dull.

627
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:57,840
他根本就没搞懂这车的精髓。
He just hasn't got the idea of this at all.

628
00:27:57,880 --> 00:27:59,560
他是怎么着，以为自己是室内设计师吗？
What is he, an interior designer, maybe?

629
00:27:59,600 --> 00:28:00,760
根本不是这回事。
- 没错。
That's not the point.
- Exactly.

630
00:28:00,800 --> 00:28:02,520
简直是不带花边袖口的劳伦斯·卢埃林-鲍恩！
Laurence Llewelyn-Bowen without the cuffs!

631
00:28:02,560 --> 00:28:04,840
它就是很酷，是你根本不懂！
It's cool. You missed it!

632
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:05,680
TVR 呢？
TVR?

633
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:07,440
观众：酷！
AUDIENCE: Cool.

634
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:10,640
才怪！你们又错了！土得掉渣！
No! Again, you're wrong! Uncool!

635
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:14,080
允许我给你们解释一下为什么，听好了好吗？
And I'll explain why, if I may, okay?

636
00:28:14,120 --> 00:28:15,880
大家都知道，TVR 这种车，
TVRs, as we know,

637
00:28:15,920 --> 00:28:18,640
就是专门给裤腰已经开始往上提的男人开的。
they're for men whose trousers
are creeping up a bit.

638
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:20,200
懂那种年纪吧？裤腰提到这儿了。
You know the time of life?
About there.

639
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:21,640
到了那种岁数……
The time of life...

640
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:24,400
乳头跟裤腰带之间的距离，
The gap between the nipple
and the waistband,

641
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:27,600
刚开始有点走下坡路了。
is just starting to come down a little bit.

642
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:29,720
所以恐怕这就是它不酷的原因。
So I'm afraid that's why it's uncool.

643
00:28:29,760 --> 00:28:32,120
还有谁对此有意见吗？
Anyone else got any objections to that?

644
00:28:32,160 --> 00:28:33,400
观众男：有。
MAN: Yes.

645
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:35,920
哈，又是你？这回又是谁啊？
Yeah, you again? Who is it now?

646
00:28:35,960 --> 00:28:37,520
观众男：我。
MAN: Me.

647
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:39,120
你瞧瞧它，多招人喜欢！
你可不能说它不酷。
Look at it, it's lovely!
You can't say that's uncool.

648
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:40,880
而且它还有黄色的！
And it comes in yellow!

649
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:43,320
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

650
00:28:43,360 --> 00:28:45,440
可香蕉也是黄的啊！这算什么鬼话？
But so do bananas! I mean what?

651
00:28:45,480 --> 00:28:47,680
只要是黄的就酷？才怪。
Everything yellow is cool? No, it's not.

652
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:52,000
说到黄色，
这辆放哪儿？一辆Polo？
Talking of yellow,
where do we put this? A Polo?

653
00:28:52,040 --> 00:28:54,560
挺酷的！不，这车很酷！
观众：才怪！
It's cool! No, that's a cool car!
AUDIENCE: No!

654
00:28:54,600 --> 00:28:56,360
大错特错！
- 挺酷的车！
Wrong, wrong, wrong!
- Cool car!

655
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:59,000
欧式潮范儿？欧式潮范儿？
Euro chic? Euro chic?

656
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:01,360
[观众嘘声]
[AUDIENCE BOOS]

657
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:03,200
你支持我吧？
- 挺酷的。
Agree with me?
- It's cool.

658
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:04,400
谢了。
- 超级酷。
Thank you.
- Very cool.

659
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:06,080
你开什么车？
What do you drive?

660
00:29:06,120 --> 00:29:07,760
Jeep牧马人运动版，但我以前
确实开过Polo！
Jeep Wrangler Sport, but I did have
a Polo before!

661
00:29:07,800 --> 00:29:10,840
Jeep牧马人虽然开起来烂透了，
但确实酷！
Jeep Wranglers are dreadful cars
but cool!

662
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:12,960
瞧，这不正是我们一直想解释的道理吗？
See, that is what we keep trying
to explain, isn't it?

663
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:16,120
开起来怎么样、看着怎么样，根本无关紧要。
It doesn't matter what they're like
to drive or look at.

664
00:29:16,160 --> 00:29:18,360
关键在于它们到底酷不酷。
- 是什么颜色也根本不重要。
It's whether they're cool or not.
- Or what colour they are.

665
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:20,680
没错。别提颜色了。看，懂了吧？
Exactly. Forget colour. Look, you see?

666
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:22,240
比如菲亚特Punto，比如高尔夫，
You've got your Fiat Punto,
you've got your Golf,

667
00:29:22,280 --> 00:29:23,640
当然，显而易见必须是汽油版的。
as long as it is a petrol, obviously.

668
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:25,320
任何欧洲小巧车型，
Anything little and European,

669
00:29:25,360 --> 00:29:27,200
雪铁龙C3，统统放进“酷”那一栏。
Citroen C3, goes in the Cool section.

670
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:28,880
你确定M3放那儿？
You sure about the M3?

671
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:30,520
只是……我刚才晃悠过去，看到它挂在那儿，
It's just... I've wandered past,
and there it is,

672
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:32,240
我心里总还是隐隐觉得，
and I just, still part of me thinks

673
00:29:32,280 --> 00:29:33,680
那地方放错了。
that's the wrong place.

674
00:29:33,720 --> 00:29:36,560
大家觉得呢，M3？
它到底酷不酷？
What do you reckon, M3?
Is that cool or not?

675
00:29:36,600 --> 00:29:38,480
那玩意儿唯一的归宿就是垫底。
The only way to put that is down.

676
00:29:38,520 --> 00:29:41,160
[笑声]
- 我下不去手！
[LAUGHTER]
- I can't!

677
00:29:41,200 --> 00:29:44,280
别动。拜托，真的让M3留在下面吧。
Leave it. Please, leave
the M3 down there, really.

678
00:29:44,320 --> 00:29:46,440
不可否认，它是辆好车。
It's a great car, make no mistake.

679
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:47,440
那个咱们待会儿再扯。
We will discuss that one later.

680
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:49,000
是辆好车，但就是不酷。
It's a great car, but uncool.

681
00:29:49,040 --> 00:29:51,360
法拉利575？
Ferrari 575?

682
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:53,040
观众：零下酷！
- 零下酷？
MAN: Sub Zero.
- Sub Zero?

683
00:29:53,080 --> 00:29:54,080
等等，那是……
Now, that's...

684
00:29:55,080 --> 00:29:56,640
谁贴上去的？
Who's put this?

685
00:29:56,680 --> 00:29:57,960
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

686
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,400
谁把保时捷Boxster
贴到“零下酷”去了？
Who's put a Porsche Boxster
in the Sub-Zero?

687
00:30:00,440 --> 00:30:02,320
是你干的，对吧？
It's you, isn't it?

688
00:30:02,360 --> 00:30:04,440
就是你，就因为你自己买了一辆？
It's you because you've got one?

689
00:30:04,480 --> 00:30:06,240
可那车真的很酷啊！
But that's such a cool car!

690
00:30:06,280 --> 00:30:07,320
我开过一辆！
I had one!

691
00:30:07,360 --> 00:30:08,800
你之前明明把它扔在“不酷”区了。
You had that in Uncool.

692
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:10,880
它确实……呃……
- 你绝不能把它扔进“不酷”区。
It is... Mmm...
- You can't put that in Uncool.

693
00:30:10,920 --> 00:30:13,040
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

694
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:16,360
不是，你听我说，我上周开了一辆，
Boxster S，新车，棒极了。
No, you see, I had one last week,
Boxster S, new car, fantastic.

695
00:30:16,400 --> 00:30:18,760
真的，那车身平衡做得无懈可击……
Really, the most beautifully balanced...

696
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:20,440
但你开着它活像个大傻叉！
- 确实。
But you look like a prat!
- Yeah.

697
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:24,320
哪有，没那么糟糕。
No, it's not that bad.

698
00:30:24,360 --> 00:30:26,280
真没那么糟糕，真的。
It's not that bad, really.

699
00:30:26,320 --> 00:30:28,880
别把M3贴进“酷”区！
Don't put the M3 in cool!

700
00:30:28,920 --> 00:30:30,040
我停不下来啊。
I can't.

701
00:30:30,080 --> 00:30:31,720
大部分车我都由着你了，
I've gone with you on most of this,

702
00:30:31,760 --> 00:30:33,600
关于M3，谁能来声援我一下？拜托了？
will somebody please back me up
on the M3? Please?

703
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:35,640
我们现场投票决定M3。
We'll have a vote on the M3.

704
00:30:35,680 --> 00:30:37,400
先不管开起来怎么样。
Forget what it's like to drive.

705
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:41,200
觉得它酷的请举手。
Hands up if you think it's cool.

706
00:30:42,440 --> 00:30:43,920
觉得它不酷的请举手。
Hands up if you think it's uncool.

707
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:46,880
显而易见，投“酷”的更多。
我赢了，谢谢各位。
Precisely, that's more for Cool.
I win, thank you.

708
00:30:46,920 --> 00:30:49,000
是啊，但这儿可不是讲民主的地方。
这儿是《Top Gear》。
Yes, but this isn't a democracy.
This is Top Gear.

709
00:30:49,040 --> 00:30:50,600
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

710
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:52,200
反正没你赢的份。
It's a lose-lose.

711
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:53,840
你输定了。
You're gonna lose.

712
00:30:53,880 --> 00:30:57,320
好了，是时候请出我们的
“廉价车大明星”了。
Now, time to put our star
in a Reasonably-Priced Car.

713
00:30:57,360 --> 00:30:58,760
今晚这位开了家餐厅，
Now this one's got a restaurant,

714
00:30:58,800 --> 00:31:01,480
他还从一家轮胎公司手里，
拿到了三颗星。
he's got three of them,
from a tyre company.

715
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:03,160
让我们见见他？女士们先生们，
Shall we meet him? Ladies and gentlemen,

716
00:31:03,200 --> 00:31:05,000
全英国最棒的大厨——
Britain's best chef,

717
00:31:05,040 --> 00:31:07,600
当然，安斯利·哈里奥特除外——
戈登·拉姆齐！
apart from Ainsley Harriott,
obviously, Gordon Ramsay!

718
00:31:11,040 --> 00:31:12,560
近来可好，戈登？
How are you, Gordon?

719
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:14,240
安斯利·哈里奥特？
Ainsley Harriot?

720
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:16,240
他算哪门子厨师。
He's not a chef.

721
00:31:16,280 --> 00:31:18,600
什么？
- 他就是个搞笑的。
What?
- He's a comedian.

722
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:21,040
克拉克森：不好意思，
安斯利·哈里奥特不算大厨吗？
CLARKSON: I'm sorry,
Ainsley Harriott is not a chef?

723
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:23,440
杰里米，他名下一家餐厅都没有。
He doesn't even have a restaurant, Jeremy.

724
00:31:23,480 --> 00:31:26,160
他就是个喜剧演员兼节目主持人。
He's a comedian and a presenter.

725
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:28,800
人家花五镑钱就能捣鼓出一顿晚饭！
He can knock up supper for a fiver!

726
00:31:28,840 --> 00:31:30,240
他还会烤肉呢。
He can barbecue food.

727
00:31:30,280 --> 00:31:33,360
他随便弄点罐头，
再加点吸尘器袋里的灰，
He gets the contents of a tin
and the hoover bag,

728
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:34,600
搅和在一块儿，
knock them together,

729
00:31:34,640 --> 00:31:36,520
五镑钱就能喂饱一家子一个月。
£5 can feed a family for a month.

730
00:31:36,560 --> 00:31:40,960
换成你，五镑钱也就买一撮欧芹叶。
You, £5 for a sprig of parsley.

731
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:44,720
行了听着，在你忙着开
大概两万五千家餐厅的空档，
Anyway, listen, in between opening,
like, 25,000 restaurants,

732
00:31:44,760 --> 00:31:47,960
呃，你居然还“端出”了四个孩子？
um, you've managed
to dish up four children?

733
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:49,120
是的。
- 所以……
Yes.
- So...

734
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:50,640
都不满四岁。
- 全都不满四岁？
Under four.
- All under four?

735
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:52,280
全都不满四岁，是啊。简直是场噩梦。
All under four, yeah. Nightmare.

736
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:54,960
真爷们儿。哇哦！
What a man. Woah!

737
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:57,320
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

738
00:31:57,360 --> 00:31:59,280
瞧瞧这个！
- 谢谢，谢谢，太感谢了。
Look at that!
- Thank you, thank you, thank you.

739
00:31:59,320 --> 00:32:01,000
好吧，现在估计早就被掏空了！
Well, it'll be empty by now!

740
00:32:01,040 --> 00:32:02,200
你有没有，呃……
Have you, uh...

741
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:03,160
你有坐垫吗？
Have you got a cushion?

742
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:04,240
有。
Yes.

743
00:32:04,280 --> 00:32:05,560
嗯，是啊，四个都不满四岁。
Um, yeah, four under four.

744
00:32:05,600 --> 00:32:08,120
那你家用什么当家用车？
So what do you do for a family car?

745
00:32:08,160 --> 00:32:11,000
家用车？开路虎揽胜还真出了点问题，
Family car? It turned out to be a bit
of a problem with a Range Rover,

746
00:32:11,040 --> 00:32:14,080
因为后排怎么都装不下四个安全座椅。
'cause we could never get
all four seats in the back.

747
00:32:14,120 --> 00:32:17,360
所以，呃，塔娜提议买辆新奔驰，
So, um, Tana came up
with the idea of buying a new Mercedes,

748
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:19,720
就提了辆六座的ML。
and got one of those ML 6-seaters.

749
00:32:19,760 --> 00:32:21,800
对，但那车后头根本没有后备箱。
Yeah, but there's no boot
in the back of it.

750
00:32:21,840 --> 00:32:23,160
后头绝对没有后备箱，真没有。
Definitely no boot in the back, no.

751
00:32:23,200 --> 00:32:24,720
不过我平时倒不太……
But I don't really get, sort of,

752
00:32:24,760 --> 00:32:26,440
深度参与这些破事儿，你懂的……
over involved with the whole,
sort of, you know...

753
00:32:26,480 --> 00:32:28,880
你不用去接送孩子上下学？
You don't do the school run?

754
00:32:28,920 --> 00:32:30,280
我就去过一次，
I did once,

755
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:31,360
简直就是一场彻头彻尾的噩梦。
and it was an absolute nightmare.

756
00:32:31,400 --> 00:32:32,760
说来听听，展开讲讲。
Go on, talk me through it.

757
00:32:32,800 --> 00:32:35,440
好吧，那是早上8点20分，你懂的，
Well, it's, you know, 8:20 in the morning,

758
00:32:35,480 --> 00:32:39,720
你开着车沿着旺兹沃思路，
往巴特西方向走。
and you're driving along the,
sort of, Wandsworth Road,
towards Battersea.

759
00:32:39,760 --> 00:32:42,640
而现在的女人……
And the women now...

760
00:32:42,680 --> 00:32:46,600
那些当妈的不仅并排双停，
她们都敢并排停三层！
The mums don't double park,
they treble park.

761
00:32:46,640 --> 00:32:49,240
不过说起来挺逗的是，
Have to say though, rather amusingly,

762
00:32:49,280 --> 00:32:50,880
几年前，
is that a few years ago,

763
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:52,120
我拍过一个节目，
I was making a programme

764
00:32:52,160 --> 00:32:55,520
是关于切尔西那些开车接送孩子的妈妈们的。
about women doing the school run
in Chelsea.

765
00:32:55,560 --> 00:32:56,640
我带着摄制组来到了
Turned up with a film crew outside

766
00:32:56,680 --> 00:32:58,920
斯隆广场的一所小学校门外，
a little school in Sloane Square,

767
00:32:58,960 --> 00:33:01,400
结果你猜谁把车开过来还并排三层违停？
who should pull up and treble park,

768
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:03,040
正是戈登·拉姆齐夫人！
but Mrs. Gordon Ramsay!

769
00:33:04,080 --> 00:33:05,400
我还以为你早忘了这事呢！
I thought you forgot about that!

770
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:06,840
哪能啊，我怎么可能忘呢？
No, of course, how could I possibly forget?

771
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:08,320
她长得特别迷人，
She's very attractive,

772
00:33:08,360 --> 00:33:11,400
而这也是我不去接送孩子的绝招，伙计们。
which is my key for not doing
the school run, chaps.

773
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:14,520
懂吧？你得这么干，先主动请缨，明白吗？
Okay? What you do, volunteer, okay?

774
00:33:14,560 --> 00:33:16,320
“今天早上我去送孩子吧。”说到做到。
"I'll do the school run
his morning." Do it.

775
00:33:16,360 --> 00:33:19,760
第二天早上，再去；第三天早上，继续去。
The next morning, do it again;
next morning, do it again.

776
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:22,280
到了第四天早上，跟你老婆说：
Fourth morning, say to your wife,

777
00:33:22,320 --> 00:33:23,560
“学校里好多学生妈妈，
"Lot of those mums at the school,

778
00:33:23,600 --> 00:33:25,200
身材可真苗条，是吧？”
quite slim, aren't they?"

779
00:33:25,240 --> 00:33:27,160
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

780
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:28,200
包你以后再也不用去了。
You'll never do it again.

781
00:33:28,880 --> 00:33:30,160
这就是我的绝招。
That's my key.

782
00:33:30,200 --> 00:33:32,400
女司机和素食主义者……
Women drivers and vegetarians...

783
00:33:32,440 --> 00:33:36,680
要是我们把拥堵费抛到脑后，改成单双日限行，
And if we could just forget these
congestion charges and have alternate days,

784
00:33:36,720 --> 00:33:39,000
一天让女司机开，一天让素食主义者开，
one for women drivers, one for vegetarians,

785
00:33:39,040 --> 00:33:41,480
在伦敦开车岂不爽翻天？是不是？
London will be a dream to drive around, no?

786
00:33:41,520 --> 00:33:43,080
这……大家觉得这提议如何？
How would this... how would this play?

787
00:33:43,120 --> 00:33:44,680
听着不错吧，你们觉得呢？
Is this good, do you think?

788
00:33:44,720 --> 00:33:46,080
男观众：那我可不去伦敦了。我是个素食主义者。
MAN: Well, I wouldn't go
to London. I'm a vegetarian.

789
00:33:46,120 --> 00:33:48,200
你是素食主义者？滚出去！
You're a vegetarian? Get out!

790
00:33:48,240 --> 00:33:49,560
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

791
00:33:49,600 --> 00:33:51,920
他……他看着可一点都不像吃素的！
He... he does not look like a vegetarian!

792
00:33:51,960 --> 00:33:54,440
对，可不是嘛。
Yeah, yeah.

793
00:33:54,480 --> 00:33:56,400
你到底跑来Top Gear干什么？《园艺世界》在汉普郡录呢。
What the hell are you doing at Top Gear?
Gardeners World is in Hampshire.

794
00:33:56,440 --> 00:33:58,480
我一直都在试图解释这点。
I keep trying to explain this.

795
00:33:58,520 --> 00:34:01,200
女人和素食主义者，我倒挺喜欢这主意。
Women and vegetarians,
I quite like that idea.

796
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:04,280
但是，我是说，他们开车也就时速15英里。
- 谁，素食主义者吗？
But, I mean, they drive, you know,
15 miles an hour.
- Who, vegetarians do?

797
00:34:04,320 --> 00:34:06,720
没错，他们开车根本不看路，
Yes, they, sort of,
don't look where they're going,

798
00:34:06,760 --> 00:34:07,880
从来不打转向灯，
they never indicate,

799
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:09,440
而且路上只要一出状况，
and the minute there's a problem
on the road,

800
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:10,840
他们直接就把方向盘撒手了。
they, sort of, let go
of the steering wheel.

801
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:12,960
你怎么能看出来
他们是吃素的？
How are you able to tell
that they're vegetarians?

802
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:15,640
关键就在这儿……
我当然愿意相信他们就是素食者。
This is the one thing...
I like to think they are, of course.

803
00:34:15,680 --> 00:34:19,280
因为他们看着就很不靠谱！
Because they just look rather dodgy!

804
00:34:19,320 --> 00:34:21,360
克拉克森：面无血色、病恹恹的那种？
CLARKSON: Sort of pale and wan?

805
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:25,280
急需来上一块带血的上好菲力牛排，
诸如此类的，你懂的。
In need of a good, bloody fillet steak and,
sort of, you know.

806
00:34:25,320 --> 00:34:28,200
好了，既然聊到路上
那些让人抓狂的破事儿，
Now, while we are on the subject of things
that annoy us on the road,

807
00:34:28,240 --> 00:34:31,040
嗯，高速公路服务区。
um, motorway service stations.

808
00:34:31,080 --> 00:34:33,560
大家肯定都去过。你们觉得
那里的饭菜怎么样？
We've all been there. What do you think
of the food?

809
00:34:33,600 --> 00:34:37,200
极其骇人、恶心透顶的油腻，
Shockingly, disgustingly fat,

810
00:34:37,240 --> 00:34:41,000
凄惨无比，一股塑料味，呃……
pretty dismal, plastic, um...

811
00:34:41,040 --> 00:34:42,280
而且贵得要命。
And expensive.

812
00:34:42,320 --> 00:34:45,520
……恶心巴拉的假冒伪劣食品。嗯……
...gross, imitation food. Um...

813
00:34:45,560 --> 00:34:47,280
所以上任何高速之前，
And before you go on
any motorway,

814
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:48,880
开车前一定先吃饱。
eat before you drive.

815
00:34:48,920 --> 00:34:51,160
不，其实搞笑的是，
开车前根本用不着吃。
No, actually, funny enough,
no need to eat before you drive.

816
00:34:51,200 --> 00:34:54,960
我们突发奇想。
我们琢磨着，等一下啊，
We had a bit of an idea.
We thought, hang on a minute,

817
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:56,400
你开着车在路上跑，
you're driving along in a car,

818
00:34:56,440 --> 00:35:00,080
车头前面可是一台滚烫的大引擎啊。
which has a big hot engine in the front.

819
00:35:00,120 --> 00:35:04,440
为什么不边开车，
边用它来把饭做熟呢？
Why not use that to cook your food
as you drive along?

820
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:07,120
所以今天早上，我们有了个主意，明白吧？
So, this morning, we had an idea, okay?

821
00:35:07,160 --> 00:35:09,200
行，我们放段录像。
来，让你们瞧瞧我们干了什么好事。
Okay, we'll just run some tape.
Here. I'll show you what we did.

822
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:11,160
这是一辆斯巴鲁森林人（Subaru Forester），
This is a Subaru Forester,

823
00:35:11,200 --> 00:35:13,440
绑在它水平对置四缸发动机上的，
and strapped to its flat four engine,

824
00:35:13,480 --> 00:35:16,920
是一块鲜嫩多汁的火鸡胸肉，
we have a succulent turkey breast

825
00:35:16,960 --> 00:35:19,440
淋着牛肝菌红酒浓缩酱汁，
in a reduction of porcini mushrooms
and red wine,

826
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:21,280
配以冬日抱子甘蓝点缀。
garnished with winter sprouts.

827
00:35:21,320 --> 00:35:23,320
还有什么能比这更诱人的！
What could be more delicious than that!

828
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:27,160
好，这辆是前些天被我们
魔改成路特斯的拉达（Lada），
Okay, this is the Lada
we turned into a Lotus the other day,

829
00:35:27,200 --> 00:35:32,120
它正被用来烹饪一份配时令蔬菜的
小羊排，
and that's being used to cook a baby rack
of lamb with market vegetables,

830
00:35:32,160 --> 00:35:36,120
拌上橄榄油和地中海香草，懂吧？
dressed in olive oil
and Mediterranean herbs, right?

831
00:35:36,160 --> 00:35:39,840
接下来是铃木Liana（Suzuki Liana），
它负责烹饪一份野生三文鱼，
Now, the Suzuki Liana,
which will be cooking a wild salmon

832
00:35:39,880 --> 00:35:44,000
铺在柠檬百里香上，
佐以“Top Gear特制炸薯条”。
on a bed of lemon thyme,
accompanied by pommes Top Gear.

833
00:35:44,040 --> 00:35:46,040
那可是素食之选。
Vegetarian option there.

834
00:35:46,080 --> 00:35:50,240
算不上，因为我们公认，吃鱼
属于“情有可原的谋杀”。
No, 'cause we recognise, we know that fish
is justifiable homicide.

835
00:35:50,280 --> 00:35:51,880
红肉，那才是罪大恶极的谋杀。
Meat, the murderous thing.

836
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:53,760
你们真在发动机上做饭啊？
You actually cook them on there?

837
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:55,840
没开玩笑，肉现在就在发动机上，
正跟着车子一路慢颠慢烤呢。
Yeah, no, they're on the engines now
as they're trundling along.

838
00:35:55,880 --> 00:35:59,160
忘掉什么燃气烤箱6档，呃，或者450度吧，
Forget gas mark 6, uh, or 450 degrees,

839
00:35:59,200 --> 00:36:00,840
在我们这儿，度量单位是发动机转速。
the measurement here is revs.

840
00:36:00,880 --> 00:36:04,960
我们建议转速维持在3000转，
开上大约两小时，行了吧？
We recommend 3,000 RPM
for about two hours, okay?

841
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,680
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

842
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:09,560
两个小时后，
So after two hours,

843
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:12,040
我叫停了一辆车，行吧？端上来了。
I pulled one of them in, okay? Here it is.

844
00:36:12,080 --> 00:36:16,000
咱们瞅瞅现在……呃，
烤得怎么样了。
Let's have a look how we're, uh...
how we're doing.

845
00:36:16,040 --> 00:36:17,720
[拉姆齐大笑]
[RAMSAY LAUGHING]

846
00:36:17,760 --> 00:36:21,080
我看肉还泛着粉呢。我，呃……
I think it's still a bit pink. I'll, uh...

847
00:36:21,120 --> 00:36:22,680
我再撒点调料，
I'll add some seasoning

848
00:36:22,720 --> 00:36:25,920
看看能不能压一压
里面的机油味儿，
see if we can mask the smell
of engine oil in there,

849
00:36:25,960 --> 00:36:29,240
然后呢，呃，我估摸着
得把它扔回赛道继续烤。
and, uh, send it back out again,
I suspect.

850
00:36:29,280 --> 00:36:32,880
这是最好的办法。后盖盖上。
这就妥了。
Best thing to do. Keep the hatch down.
There we go.

851
00:36:32,920 --> 00:36:36,680
回赛道去吧。或者说回烤肉架去，
我们平时都这么叫。
Get back on the track. Or the rotisserie
as we like to call it.

852
00:36:38,440 --> 00:36:40,920
所以呢，我们大致算了一下，
So, really, we kinda worked it out

853
00:36:40,960 --> 00:36:43,480
如果你从伦敦出发，
that if you were to set off from London,

854
00:36:43,520 --> 00:36:46,080
也就是你的住处，开去利兹，
from where you live, going to Leeds,

855
00:36:46,120 --> 00:36:49,280
等你开到谢菲尔德附近的伍德尔服务区时，
by the time you get to Woodall services
near Sheffield,

856
00:36:49,320 --> 00:36:51,960
午饭差不多就能出锅了，对吧？
lunch should be about ready, okay?

857
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:55,440
所以今天早上一帮车在我们赛道上
慢悠悠转悠了两个小时，
So they were trundling around
our track this morning for two hours,

858
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:57,960
斯提格在吗？
and is The Stig here?

859
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:00,480
我们终于大发慈悲
让他别在寒风里冻着了，
We've finally allowed him
to come out of the cold,

860
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:02,360
特批他进了演播室大本营。
and we've allowed him into the base.

861
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:03,600
你能把那吃的端过来吗？
Can you bring the food over?

862
00:37:03,640 --> 00:37:04,960
他来了，女士们先生们，
Here he is, ladies and gentlemen,

863
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:08,600
破天荒头一遭
亲临演播室——斯提格！
for the first time ever,
in the studio, The Stig!

864
00:37:08,640 --> 00:37:09,720
大餐来了！
Here it is!

865
00:37:15,960 --> 00:37:20,280
来，呃，你尝尝
那份三文鱼怎么样？
Now, um, why don't you sample
some of that salmon?

866
00:37:20,320 --> 00:37:22,400
给评价评价。
Tell me what you think.

867
00:37:22,440 --> 00:37:23,960
拉姆齐：这真是
在发动机上烤熟的？
RAMSAY: This was actually cooked
on the engine?

868
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:26,440
就包着锡纸？
- 真的，千真万确，这里所有吃的
In tin foil?
- It was, genuinely, all of this food

869
00:37:26,480 --> 00:37:28,000
都是在汽车发动机上做熟的。
was cooked on the engine of the car.

870
00:37:28,040 --> 00:37:31,760
你给说说，这能不能赶上
高速公路服务区的手艺？
Tell me if that matches up
to motorway service cooking.

871
00:37:31,800 --> 00:37:33,680
那绝对赶得上，毫无悬念。
It certainly matches it. Yes, definitely.

872
00:37:33,720 --> 00:37:35,640
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

873
00:37:37,080 --> 00:37:38,400
有点发干，
That is slightly dry,

874
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:40,080
稍微火候过了点，还有，呃……
a little bit overcooked, and, um...

875
00:37:41,440 --> 00:37:43,000
所以够不上米其林三星？
So not worthy of three stars?

876
00:37:43,040 --> 00:37:44,360
两星呢？
Two stars?

877
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:46,280
我连……呃，我都不想给……
I wouldn't even give that, um...

878
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:48,240
一……一星？
- 我连一星都绝不可能给，
坚决不给。
One... One star?
- I wouldn't even give that
one star, definitely not.

879
00:37:48,280 --> 00:37:49,880
连一星都不给啊。
- 不给。
Not even one star.
- No.

880
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,320
行吧，尝尝这块羊肉。
Well, try a bit of lamb.

881
00:37:51,360 --> 00:37:53,440
尝块羊肉吧，
顺便提醒各位一句，
Try a bit of lamb,
and just to remind everybody,

882
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:56,400
这玩意儿，呃，是在拉达发动机上烤的。
this was, uh, cooked on the Lada.

883
00:37:56,440 --> 00:38:00,280
菜市场买的时蔬，呃，
淋了橄榄油，撒了地中海香草。
Market vegetables, uh,
dressed in olive oil, Mediterranean herbs.

884
00:38:00,320 --> 00:38:01,760
这可是你喜欢的调调啊，老兄！
That's your sort of food, mate!

885
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:03,600
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

886
00:38:03,640 --> 00:38:05,280
你觉得他喜欢的这口怎么样？
What do you think of his sort of food?

887
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:06,960
[轻笑]
[CHUCKLES]

888
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:09,440
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

889
00:38:09,480 --> 00:38:11,760
我看戈登快要吐出来了！
I think Gordon is about to be sick!

890
00:38:14,120 --> 00:38:14,960
你也尝点。
You have some.

891
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:17,040
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

892
00:38:17,080 --> 00:38:18,720
来几颗抱子甘蓝。
Have some sprouts.

893
00:38:22,520 --> 00:38:25,960
连吃素的都咽不下去！
Not even the vegetarian likes it!

894
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:29,440
而且吃起来一股汽油味！
